\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:conclusion}

We showed that knowledge conflict signals in multilingual LLMs are linearly detectable across languages, with the ZH$\to$EN transfer advantage (${\sim}$7~pp) consistent with the XNLI baseline.
Causal influence localizes to Llama L13 while detection peaks at L28; steering fails in Qwen and Gemma despite 0.93 AUROC, showing detectability does not imply causal relevance.

